A||N||4||gmata||Sunroof rivets||||5||
Z||000000||gmata||10-07-2001||02:54 PM||||I'm trying to replace my old rusted sunroof channels.  I remove the old channels by drilling out the rivets.  When installing the new channels, do I really need to rivet the channels down?  If I need to use rivets, what size and how do you install rivets?<P>Also, I have been reading the postings about drilling drain holes within the sunroof. But, I must be stupid since I'm still puzzled on where exactly the holes should be drilled.  Are the holes drilled on the inside corner( towards the middle of the roof) or on the outside corner ).  Do I drill at an angle?<P>Thanks,<BR>Gus<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-07-2001||09:21 PM||||Yes you need rivit back down the channels, just regular aluminum pop rivets.  In order to get all the channels out you will have to take down the headliner and unscrew some of the screws that hold the roof down, because some of the channels have bolt bosses for them.  You will also probably have to use some backer plates for the pop rivits, at least that's what I had to do.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||10-07-2001||09:27 PM||||Sorry, forgot about the holes.<P>When you pull off your rubber gasket, you'll see those channels.  Where they come together at the corners there is a space where there isnt any channel and the gasket is usually glued down in this area.  You will want to drill about an 1/8" hole in the lowest part of the corner there, towards the back of the car.  The water actually drains out through the rear of the car becuase of the slope.  Once you have the holes in the fiberglass top the water will run down the steel roof until it gets into the drain hole that runs down the b-pillar.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||10-07-2001||09:27 PM||||DP<p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||4BanGinFun||10-07-2001||10:34 PM||||in my fiero the water leaks in around the sunroof and runs down the front pilers and inside the car onto both the psngr and driver side floor will drain holes fix this problem?? where do the drain holes go exacually?? is ther a pic somewhere showing where to drill and how to drill?? any other solutions?? will the water running down rot the steel frame?? <p>[This message has been edited by 4BanGinFun (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
